WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.020
The carpal tunnel is a narrow passage in the
wrist.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:26.690
It is formed by wrist bones on the bottom
and sides and a tough band of connective tissue,

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:32.920
called the transverse carpal ligament, on
top.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:38.800
Muscle tendons and the median nerve pass through
the carpal tunnel.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:46.150
The median nerve controls muscles in the palm
and base of the thumb, allowing them to move.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:53.880
It also provides feeling to the thumb and
nearby two and a half fingers.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.510
Carpal tunnel syndrome is a condition where
tissue swelling causes pressure to build up

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.420
within the carpal tunnel.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.930
This puts pressure on the median nerve.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:12.150
Over time median nerve pressures results in
symptoms in the areas of hand it supplies.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:22.119
Common symptoms in these areas are pain, numbness,
tingling, and weakness.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:28.049
Risk factors for carpal tunnel syndrome include
a smaller carpal tunnel from being female

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:38.689
or from genes passed down from parents, wrist
injuries, other medical conditions that cause

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:45.780
inflammation, fluid buildup, or nerve damage
such as diabetes, pregnancy, rheumatoid arthritis,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:57.929
obesity, and hypothyroidism, and repetitive
hand or wrist motions.

00:01:57.929 --> 00:02:02.700
A common treatment for mild to moderate carpal
tunnel syndrome is keeping the wrist in a

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:09.170
neutral position by wearing a brace or splint.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:18.110
In addition, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory
drugs, or NSAIDs, may help relieve pain.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:26.140
A doctor may recommend a corticosteroid injection
to reduce inflammation and swelling.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.940
For moderate to severe symptoms, a doctor
may recommend a surgical procedure called

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.130
carpal tunnel release.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:39.640
This procedure may be done as an open procedure
through an incision between the palm and wrist,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:46.050
or it may be done as an endoscopic procedure
through a small keyhole incision.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.470
The surgeon will perform this procedure with
an endoscope, which is a device containing

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.181
a tiny camera and surgical instruments.

00:02:52.181 --> 00:03:00.410
In both procedures the transverse carpal ligament
will be cut to relieve pressure on the median

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.900
nerve.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:07.180
At the end of either procedure the incision
will be closed with sutures.

